 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+The non-Error rejection behaviour remains outside the scope of both #36 and #93.
 
 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
+
+## Turn usage — #93 acceptance contract
+
+The chosen shape keeps one usage argument and sums provider calls, rather than adding a per-round breakdown: the hook serves turn-level billing and budgeting, and no additional provider-call API is needed for that purpose. These tests specify the pending change; their citations do not claim it is implemented. The public hook signature must identify the value as total turn usage, with a MINOR release and a changelog entry explaining the larger values existing consumers will record on tool-heavy turns.
+
+- `afterModelResponse` fires once after two tool rounds and receives the sum of input, output and total tokens from all three provider calls ([validated by: reports the sum of every provider call after two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L61)).
+- Missing usage on any round contributes nothing to the sum; reported rounds still count, an entirely unreported turn yields `undefined`, and reported zero usage remains zero ([validated by: sums reported rounds when usage is missing and preserves absent usage when none report](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L71)).
+- A turn without tool calls retains its existing response text and usage ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
